00:10:36.464 --> 00:10:37.837
&gt;&gt; Uh-huh.

00:10:37.838 --> 00:10:41.010
&gt;&gt; Which peers does?

00:10:41.011 --> 00:10:44.180
&gt;&gt; So that's a great question.

00:10:44.181 --> 00:10:48.042
So substance abuse happens prior
to people becoming homeless, and

00:10:48.043 --> 00:10:50.720
it could be a cause of
homelessness as well.

00:10:50.721 --> 00:10:53.412
So a lot of people
become homeless,

00:10:53.413 --> 00:10:56.287
because they're
substance users and

00:10:56.288 --> 00:11:00.148
also because they have to
survive in an environment

00:11:00.149 --> 00:11:04.300
where drug abuse is considered
to be a survival skill.

00:11:04.301 --> 00:11:07.852
It could get exacerbated because
of the circumstances they face

00:11:07.853 --> 00:11:10.400
after they experience
homelessness.

00:11:10.401 --> 00:11:12.080
So it could be both.

00:11:12.081 --> 00:11:15.760
It's a chicken and egg thing.

